            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure relates to a sole structure (200) for an article of footwear (10), the sole structure (200) comprising: a bladder (206) having a chamber (220) including (i) an arcuate segment (226) extending around a heel region (16) of the sole structure (200), (ii) a first segment (228) in fluid communication with the arcuate segment (226) and extending along a medial side (22) of the sole structure (200) from the arcuate segment (226) to a first terminal end (234a) in a forefoot region (12), and (iii) a second segment (230) in fluid communication with the arcuate segment (226), spaced apart from the first segment (228) across a width of the sole structure (200), and extending along a lateral side (24) of the sole structure (200) from the arcuate segment (226) to a second terminal end (234b) in the forefoot region (12); and an outer cushion (210) extending continuously around an outer perimeter of the sole structure (200) to form a closed loop, the outer cushion (210) including a top surface (284) and a bottom surface (286) disposed on an opposite side of the outer cushion (210) than the top surface (284), the bottom surface (286) opposing and being in contact with the first segment (228), the second segment (230), and the arcuate segment (226) of the bladder (206) along the entire length of the chamber (220).</p>
            </abstract>
